{"toolCallId":"call_3db9853f3ea14d279ee5eae65d91ff1d","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-008 | REQ-007 | Given a run whose warning goes to stderr, When `--quiet` is passed, Then the warning still reaches stderr and only stdout is trimmed | `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value`, and `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>/dev/null` prints the single level line | Unmet | - |\nspec.md:98:| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr: the flag trims stdout only and never redirects, merges or suppresses fd 2. |\ntasks.md:53:- [ ] T017 Implement REQ-007: confine the quiet guard to stdout and leave fd 2 untouched, so a warning still reaches stderr (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value` and `rg -n '2>&1' $S` prints nothing.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"316b63","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
